    "problem_statement": "Dict `|` operator returns NotImplemented for valid dict types\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `|` (union) operator for Dict objects is incorrectly returning `NotImplemented` when used with valid dictionary types (both `Dict` and regular `dict` instances).\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom addict import Dict\n\n# This should work but returns NotImplemented\nd1 = Dict({'a': 1})\nd2 = Dict({'b': 2})\nresult = d1 | d2\nprint(result)  # Expected: Dict({'a': 1, 'b': 2}), Actual: NotImplemented\n\n# Same issue with regular dict\nd3 = {'c': 3}\nresult2 = d1 | d3\nprint(result2)  # Expected: Dict({'a': 1, 'c': 3}), Actual: NotImplemented\n```\n\nThe union operator should merge the dictionaries and return a new Dict instance, but instead it's returning `NotImplemented` for all dictionary-like objects."
  },
